      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Table printed sideways on the page (rotated 90°). '..' is printed in the source for nil/no entry; cells left \"\" (and not listed as unreadable) are where nothing at all is printed: Chihli Iron and Mercury, Shantung Iron Ore, Turkestan Zinc, Ch'uanpien Zinc and Iron Ore, Jehol and Suiyüan Antimony, and the blank second-line cells.",
        "The print is skewed: figures in the right-hand columns sit up to ~20 px above their row labels; rows were assigned by following each line across the columns.",
        "Hunan, Total tonnage, Unit Value and Total Value have a second printed line; each is given as a following row with an empty label (Hunan second line: Lead 'Ore 9,684', Zinc 27,242, Iron 35,400, Iron Ore 106,000, Antimony 'Regulus 10,000').",
        "Antimony entries are printed with the word 'Crude' or 'Regulus' on the line above the figure; given as 'Crude 500' etc.",
        "Spaces in place of commas are as printed ('14 400', '69 000', '1 200', '2 600', '27 242', '1,634 000', '16,000 000'). Some commas print like points at scan resolution (e.g. Hunan Gold 4,440, Hunan Iron 35,400, Lead total 1,441) and are given as commas.",
        "Row 'Chekiang', col 'Manganese Ore': unreadable — no clear mark, only a faint speck where '..' would be.",
        "Row 'Yünnan', col 'Iron Ore': unreadable — printed '28,0?0', the tens digit is damaged.",
        "Row 'Total tonnage', col 'Gold': unreadable — printed '?08,630', first digit damaged (1 or 2).",
        "Row 'Unit Value' (second line), col 'Lead': unreadable — printed '?0', first digit damaged (looks like 8).",
        "Row 'Total Value', col 'Iron Ore': unreadable — printed like '1,39,0?00§' with broken type. The § refers to the footnote '§ Export only.'",
        "Row 'Total Value', col 'Manganese Ore': unreadable — printed '5?6,000', middle digit damaged.",
        "Row 'Total Value', col 'Mercury': unreadable — printed '1,?44 000', the digit after the comma is damaged (1 or 4).",
        "Silver Unit Value '..' is followed by an ink blot, ignored.",
        "Totals (own addition, reading spaced figures as numbers; validator cannot parse '2 600' etc.): Gold total unreadable (parts sum to 108,630); Silver parts sum 29,200 — reconciles; Lead: province figures sum 1,440 vs printed 1,441 — does NOT reconcile (diff 1), and Lead ore 9,684 reconciles; Zinc 1,360 and 27,242 reconcile; Copper parts sum 1,341 vs printed 1,342 — does NOT reconcile (diff 1); Iron parts 355,750 — reconciles; Iron Ore: parts excluding unreadable Yünnan sum 1,310,520 vs 1,338,520 — not checkable; Manganese Ore 12,900 reconciles; Tin total printed '..' although provinces show 10+350+7,500+300 = 8,160 — as printed; Antimony Regulus 10,000+400 = 10,400 reconciles, Crude 500+14,500+500+300+300 = 16,100 reconciles; Mercury 314, Molybdenum 2, Tungsten 2,000 reconcile. Lead and Copper cells were re-read once; readings stand. Validator SUM lines mixing first and second lines are false mismatches.",
        "29 data rows counted on the page (26 provinces + Total tonnage, Unit Value, Total Value); 29 transcribed, plus 4 second-line rows (Hunan, Total tonnage, Unit Value, Total Value) and the 'Province:' heading row."
      ],
